<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43535" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖγε</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖ
			γε</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well, rightly</i>, in replies
			confirming or approving what has been said: as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοὶ γὰρ χαρίζομαι</span>. Answ. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖγε σὺ ποιῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					351c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖγ᾽, εὖγε ποιήσαντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					285
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖγε, εὖγε, ὦ κύνες, ἕπεσθε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyn.</u>
					6.19
				</span></i>
			: iron., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖ γοῦν θίγοις ἂν χερνίβων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1602
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖγε μέντἂν διετέθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1692
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> without a
			Verb, <i>good! well said! well done</i>! <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				494c
			</span></i>, al.; doubled 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖγ᾽, εὖγε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					470
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖγ᾽</span>, 
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖγε, νὴ Δἴ, εὖγε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ec.</u>
					213
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖγ᾽, ὅτι ἐπείσθης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					866
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖγε τῆς προαιρέσεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Vit.Auct.</u>
					8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
